 Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b856d6cb-8174-5aa9-a3f8-f8dad2890a2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/ecf914db233f7b1775f49b060470af6a244f8ea8d101fdcced746144b0284552.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301641} {:answer/id #uuid "28598f38-b560-5ca5-b3e4-ce69e9681e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/f3cd046f58b44ee916b85df91382a16360895b12c8d47a4a25deffe09f7d7c05.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301642} {:answer/id #uuid "87a98be6-40dc-5031-9ee6-95c18bd52820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/9e5fb2564eb1f5adb380d70e1a86925fa377f10cc653d98d73ba64bfb03de197.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301643} {:answer/id #uuid "dcac7630-1451-5a75-957f-4817e5cdc8f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/e3f30779c39c3800ed3a8f090df581bc9d1b7007e299fd4504180e7be1ec52e9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301644} {:answer/id #uuid "5b5e626c-565a-5591-b6fe-eaaca7b2e1d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/2733af9666ca54ca578eea56a5f05d5d8245df01f7aa1312e70610ae8a7beee7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcac7630-1451-5a75-957f-4817e5cdc8f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/e3f30779c39c3800ed3a8f090df581bc9d1b7007e299fd4504180e7be1ec52e9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301644} :answer-field/id #uuid "67e2cbb2-6ddf-532c-9b2e-3c7e0043fe9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301640}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c6ddb24-c52e-5856-abf5-27a3d99136c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-16196" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi \n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$ This gives\n\n| **$\\theta $** | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ | $\\pi $ | $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$ This gives\n\n| **$\\theta $** | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ | $\\pi $ | $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/47615688bf550384de29a5e7e480bdab699b8eee994e5e28052e4d043e2db503.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512" :knowledge-point/title "Filling a Table of Values for a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "064dada6-813e-5fa4-8e1b-1c9a28bc69a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "064dada6-813e-5fa4-8e1b-1c9a28bc69a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301648} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bc03e44-c691-5927-b19c-cefe4658eefe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301647} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2a9454b-3567-54e1-824c-9a76f9e00dee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2a9454b-3567-54e1-824c-9a76f9e00dee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301650} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8fb061e-80e8-540a-87a4-ed021b4b7a69" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301649} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7cfb2a80-fa63-5a5c-8b2b-eaad187b6a42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cfb2a80-fa63-5a5c-8b2b-eaad187b6a42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301652} :answer-field/id #uuid "ede85813-e8f1-5d08-9ccb-18f26453d2af" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6aebe50f-dc47-519c-b6ab-6e3d67578350" :question/math-academy-id "q-326251" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{\\,t+4\\,},\\,y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t,\\,-3\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-1}} | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{5}$ | $\\sqrt{6}$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{33}{2}$ | $8$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(-3),$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $x=\\sqrt{\\,t+4\\,}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(-3)=\\sqrt{-3+4}=\\sqrt{1}=1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(-1),$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(-1)=\\frac{3}{2}(-1)^{2}-(-1)=\\frac{3}{2}+1=\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{2}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(2)=\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{2}-(2)=6-2=4.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{5}$ | $\\sqrt{6}$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{33}{2}$ | $8$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $4$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cddc940d-2185-569c-a62b-b507e95d3c35" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Range of a Parametric Equation Defined in Terms of Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ef42b53-c947-565c-92f4-0805416a3f83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\le x\\le 5,\\,-9\\le y\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301710} {:answer/id #uuid "d29e53c2-1b0f-5cc4-97e9-ccec68455ed5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\le x\\le 0,\\,1\\le y\\le 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301711} {:answer/id #uuid "72f9f89e-712b-5ab7-a5c4-cc178ff9b7af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\le x\\le 13,\\,3\\le y\\le 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301712} {:answer/id #uuid "31684924-c9a6-510c-9776-e96f4ceef062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0\\le x\\le 5,\\,-7\\le y\\le 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301713} {:answer/id #uuid "969c2915-2689-5624-bfb9-1ac9afca9aee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\le x\\le 6,\\,-13\\le y\\le -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "969c2915-2689-5624-bfb9-1ac9afca9aee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\le x\\le 6,\\,-13\\le y\\le -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301714} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea0f38ba-c575-54aa-a792-f2d49224cee9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2602fecb-27f9-522e-9ca3-fc225206d948" :question/math-academy-id "q-70523" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +5,\\,\\,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -7,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1+5 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +5\\le 1+5 \\\\ 4 & \\le x\\le 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $4\\le x\\le 6.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -6 & \\le 6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 6 \\\\ -6-7 & \\le 6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -7\\le 6-7 \\\\ -13 & \\le y\\le -1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-13\\le y\\le -1.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $4\\le x\\le 6$ and $-13\\le y\\le -1.$"}]}
